# Unity .gitignore — based on github/gitignore Unity.gitignore template.
# Placed at the repo root before Unity first generates Library/ etc.

/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
# F8 triage inbox (runtime artifacts; keep README)
!/logs/
!/logs/f8-inbox/
logs/f8-inbox/*
!logs/f8-inbox/README.md
# WO-1200 seat mailbox (UI -> CLI return path). Same shape as the F8 inbox and for the same
# reason: the CONTRACT is tracked, the TRAFFIC is not. Delivery does not need git -- the UI
# seat writes into this same working tree (see the README) -- and untracked message bodies
# keep a mailbox from becoming a publishing channel.
!/logs/seat-mail/
logs/seat-mail/*
!logs/seat-mail/README.md
# orchestration-cadence.ps1 timer stamp (machine-local, rewritten every 5 min)
logs/orchestration-cadence.stamp
# WO-1175 Discord channel pins. MACHINE-LOCAL BY DEFINITION: the pin records
# which webhook/channel THIS clone was set up against. Tracking one would make a
# fresh clone with a different .env.local refuse its own channel, which is the
# opposite of what the guard is for. It is a SHA-256 prefix, not a secret, and
# it still must not travel.
# and the directory is spelled BOTH ways on this case-insensitive filesystem
# (Logs/ from Unity, logs/ from the tools), which is why line 9 already uses a
# bracket class. A lowercase-only rule would miss the Unity spelling.
[Ll]ogs/ops-channel/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/

# MemoryCaptures can get excessive in size.
# They also could contain extremely sensitive data.
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/

# Recordings can get excessive in size.
/[Rr]ecordings/

# Autogenerated Jetbrains Rider plugin.
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*

# Visual Studio cache directory.
.vs/

# Gradle cache directory.
.gradle/

# Autogenerated VS/MD/Consulo solution and project files.
ExportedObj/
.consulo/
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# Unity3D generated meta files.
*.pidb.meta
*.pdb.meta
*.mdb.meta

# Unity3D generated file on crash reports.
sysinfo.txt

# Build artifacts (owner-test builds only — never committed).
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.app

# Crashlytics generated file.
crashlytics-build.properties

# Packed Addressables.
/[Aa]ssets/[Aa]ddressableAssetsData/*/*.bin*

# Temporary auto-generated Android Assets.
/[Aa]ssets/[Ss]treamingAssets/aa.meta
/[Aa]ssets/[Ss]treamingAssets/aa/*

# OS / editor noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Solana / wallet secrets — never commit keypairs or seed phrases (spec Part 10).
*.keypair.json
**/secrets/
*.seed

# Vercel deploy token for the dedicated build machine — machine-local secret, never commit.
.vercel-token
.vercel-token.*
.vercel/

# Transient LAN transfer credential (laptop SMB) — machine-local, never commit.
.laptop-cred

# Claude Code — local permission grant is personal/machine-scoped, not committed.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Unity batchmode build/test artifacts (regenerated; never committed).
/unity-*.log
/*-test-results.xml

# Imported KayKit art packs (~1.5 GB). Owner copies these in locally; they are
# not redistributable and far too bulky for the repo. The scene BUILDERS under
# Assets/Editor/ are the source of truth — they reconstruct the scenes from
# whatever KayKit models are present. (Owner instruction 2026-05-18:
# "exclude not needed files from the assets during check in".)
# EXCEPTION: the optimized People NPC pack (DEF-91) IS committed via LFS after a
# source-shrink pass (~90 MB) - see NpcPackSourceCompressor / NpcPackTrimmer.
/Assets/Models/*
!/Assets/Models/People/
# ...but not the redundant CGTrader mesh exports (Unity imports only the .fbx).
/Assets/Models/People/**/*.obj
/Assets/Models/People/**/*.obj.meta
/Assets/Models/People/**/*.ma
/Assets/Models/People/**/*.ma.meta
/Assets/Models/People/**/*.mtl
/Assets/Models/People/**/*.mtl.meta

# Owner Tripo art — large FBX kept local (same policy as Models/). The builder
# bakes them by path; on a fresh clone re-copy from the owner's source folder
# (the Portal falls back to a box doorway, buildings would need the re-copy).
/Assets/Art/TripoStructures/
/Assets/Art/TripoStructures.meta
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED (2026-08-07): /Assets/Art/People/CraftPix/ - the 14
# CraftPix medieval townsfolk FBX + their single shared atlas + License.txt, staged
# by hand from the owner's download and consumed by CraftPixPeopleBuilder ->
# Assets/Resources/NPCs/CraftPixPeople/*.prefab -> CastleTownsfolkInjector.BodyPool.
# This is owner-downloaded art that is NOT re-derivable from any pack: ignoring it
# would mean it exists on exactly one disk, and every other clone would spawn grey
# capsule placeholders in the town (same class as the Resources/Structures debt
# documented below and the 183 gitignored VFX dependencies fixed 2026-08-05).
# NO rule in this file matches that path today, so no negation is required - the
# note exists so a future blanket /Assets/Art/ ignore does not silently kill it.
# (.gitattributes routes *.fbx + *.png through LFS, so it travels as pointers.)
# NOTE the trailing /* rather than a bare /: git NEVER DESCENDS into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a `!` negation on a file inside `/Assets/Resources/Structures/` was
# silently dead - `git check-ignore -v` blamed line 121 for every owner-sourced FBX the
# negations below were written to rescue. Excluding the CONTENTS (/*) instead keeps the
# same mirror ignored while letting the per-asset negations actually re-include.
/Assets/Resources/Structures/*
/Assets/Resources/Structures.meta

# ...EXCEPT art the owner sourced herself, which lives nowhere else.
# The blanket ignore above exists because Resources/Structures is a MIRROR of the
# gitignored Polyperfect/Tripo packs (see CatalogPrefabImporter) - re-derivable on any
# machine that has the packs. An asset the owner downloaded and dropped in is NOT
# re-derivable: ignoring it means it exists on exactly one disk, and a fresh clone
# renders the structure that references it as a missing prefab. That is the same class
# of defect as the 183 gitignored VFX dependencies fixed on 2026-08-05.
# Un-ignore per asset, deliberately, so the mirror stays ignored and owner art does not.
# Folders need BOTH the folder and its .meta, and the negation must re-open the folder
# before a file inside it can be matched.
# Jeweler — owner-sourced Tripo art, replaced the 160 KB placeholder 2026-08-17. .fbx
# overwritten in place, .meta KEPT so the GUID survives. The Jeweler is one of the six
# NPCs that earns its door (it opens the jewelry-crafting bench, which nothing else does)
# and it anchors the rough-stone economy.
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/jeweler.fbx
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/jeweler.fbx.meta
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/jeweler.fbm/
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/jeweler.fbm.meta
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/jeweler.fbm/**
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/jeweler.prefab
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/jeweler.prefab.meta
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/jeweler.mat
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/jeweler.mat.meta

# RealmStore — owner-sourced Tripo art for PROD-003, the game's DEDICATED monetization
# storefront. Staged 2026-08-17.
# ⚠ THIS ONE IS NOT LIKE THE OTHERS AND MUST NOT BE ADDED TO THE BUILD CATALOG. Per the
# owner's ruling it is baked into the hub at a FIXED location and is NOT destructible:
# a store that can be sold, moved or destroyed is a store that can go OFFLINE, which
# turns revenue into a function of whether the last raid wave reached one building.
# It is world furniture, like the Heart — not a placeable structure.
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/RealmStore.fbx
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/RealmStore.fbx.meta
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/RealmStore.fbm/
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/RealmStore.fbm.meta
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/RealmStore.fbm/**
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/RealmStore.prefab
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/RealmStore.prefab.meta
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/RealmStore.mat
!/Assets/Resources/Structures/RealmStore.mat.meta

# Forge (the WEAPONSMITH — vendors.json: forge sells categories=[weapon]) — owner-sourced
# Tripo art, replaced the 64 KB placeholder 2026-08-17. .fbx overwritten in place, .meta
# KEPT so the GUID survives.
# ⚠ THE FILE IS CALLED Forge.fbx AND THE BUILDING SELLS WEAPONS. Do not "correct" either
# to match the other without reading vendors.json first — see the displayName defect noted
