# Low Poly Ultimate Pack (polyperfect) — 246MB asset pack kept LOCAL (owner
# instruction 2026-05-29: "use what you like and we can not git the others").
# Only the SPECIFIC prefabs/meshes we use are committed, copied into a tracked
# Resources/ path; on a fresh clone re-import the pack from the Asset Store.
/Assets/polyperfect/
/Assets/polyperfect.meta

# Supercyan "Character Pack: Fantasy" — Asset-Store char/anim pack kept LOCAL
# (same policy as polyperfect, 2026-06-14). Provides troop/hero test bodies +
# ~310 Humanoid anims. Only the SC_Footman/SC_Archer variants we use live in a
# tracked Resources/ path. On a fresh clone: re-import the pack from the Asset
# Store, then run Defenders/Art/Fix Supercyan URP Materials (converts Built-in
# shaders -> URP so it isn't magenta). See docs/SUPERCYAN_REIMPORT.md.
/Assets/Supercyan/*
/Assets/Supercyan.meta

# EXCEPTION (PROD-019, 2026-08-30): track the IMPORT SETTINGS of the gear meshes,
# never the art. `isReadable: 0` on Fantasy_Shield.FBX is invisible in the Editor
# — Unity keeps mesh data CPU-side there, so mesh.vertices reads fine — but in a
# PLAYER BUILD a non-readable mesh returns ZERO vertices. EquipmentController's
# ShieldHandleSide measures the mesh to decide which face points outward; with no
# vertices it skips the flip entirely and the plate lands strap/edge-inward, flush
# to the arm. That is the "shield renders but is unreadable on device" defect that
# cost an evening: it CANNOT be seen in Play mode, only on a device.
# Tracking just the .meta (a ~2 KB text file) makes `isReadable: 1` survive a
# clone while no paid-pack binary ever enters git history.
# ⚠ ON A FRESH CLONE, RE-IMPORT THE PACK BEFORE OPENING UNITY. A tracked .meta
# with no asset beside it is an orphan, and Unity deletes orphan .meta files —
# which would silently restore the defect with no diff to explain it.
!/Assets/Supercyan/Models/
/Assets/Supercyan/Models/*
!/Assets/Supercyan/Models/Fantasy/
/Assets/Supercyan/Models/Fantasy/*
!/Assets/Supercyan/Models/Fantasy/Fantasy_Shield.FBX.meta

