# Generated config
Assets/Generated/*

# EXCEPT the terrain material (RCA 2026-07-15 — the magenta ground).
# Main_Castle_Overworld.unity:16016 references this material BY GUID
# (0eb083914b7ffae4eaf721e2353fea0b). Ignoring it meant the .mat was NEVER IN GIT — verified:
# `git log --all -- Assets/Generated/Terrain/ExteriorTerrainMaterial.mat` returns EMPTY. It only
# ever existed as a bake artifact on whichever machine last ran the terrain bake, so on every
# other machine the GUID dangled, materialTemplate resolved to NULL, and the Terrain drew with
# the engine default = MAGENTA under URP.
# The asymmetry that hid this for so long: ExteriorTerrainData.asset + the 5 .terrainlayer files
# ARE tracked (committed BEFORE this ignore rule landed), so the terrain geometry/collider always
# survived — the ground was walkable, just magenta.
# A TRACKED SCENE MUST NOT REFERENCE AN IGNORED ASSET. Tracking the material also guarantees the
# build retains URP/Terrain/Lit's shader VARIANTS (a material serialized into a built scene is what
# exempts them from URP's m_StripUnusedVariants).
# SCOPE: the WHOLE Terrain bake folder, not just the .mat — every file in it is bake output the
# scene binds by GUID, so a missing .terrainlayer would reproduce this exact bug with a different
# symptom. 14 of its 16 files were already tracked; this makes the set complete and consistent.
# Other Assets/Generated/* subfolders stay ignored (they are not scene-referenced).
!Assets/Generated/Terrain/

