# EXCEPTION (WO-1284, 2026-08-30): track the IMPORT SETTINGS of the weapon meshes,
# never the art. 400 of the 417 gear meshes shipped with `isReadable: 0`, i.e. the
# ENTIRE equippable weapon catalogue. That flag is invisible in the Editor — Unity
# keeps mesh data CPU-side there — but a player build gets ZERO vertices, so
# EquipmentController's SheatheSign / ShieldHandleSide silently skip their flip and
# the prop is worn edge/strap-inward. The device trace called Read/Write-OFF "the
# SHIPPED state of the live weapons"; it was the catalogue default, not one asset.
# Cost PROD-019 an evening against a seat that was never wrong.
# A directory rule, deliberately, NOT a list of 400 names: a copied list goes stale
# the first time someone adds a weapon, which is the exact drift CLAUDE.md §2/§5
# were written about. ~2 KB of text each, no paid-pack binary enters git history.
# ⚠ ON A FRESH CLONE, RE-IMPORT THE PACK BEFORE OPENING UNITY. A tracked .meta with
# no asset beside it is an orphan, and Unity deletes orphan .meta files — silently
# restoring the defect with no diff to explain it.
!/Assets/Blink/Art/
/Assets/Blink/Art/*
!/Assets/Blink/Art/Weapons/
/Assets/Blink/Art/Weapons/*
!/Assets/Blink/Art/Weapons/LowPoly/
/Assets/Blink/Art/Weapons/LowPoly/*
