# *.tripo-extracted — UN-IGNORED 2026-08-20. These are NOT build droppings; they are the
# ONLY opt-out TripoAssetPostprocessor.OnPreprocessModel honours. Without a sentinel it
# force-sets materialLocation=External + materialName=BasedOnTextureName on EVERY import of
# every FBX under EnemyContent, which IGNORES the externalObjects remap table and resolves
# materials by TEXTURE NAME instead. All four AccuRig skeletons name their diffuse
# 'Material_Pbr_Diffuse', so they collapse onto one material and seven enemy ids end up
# wearing the Mage's skin (measured 2026-08-20).
# Ignoring these made the fix local-only: on a fresh clone the sentinels are absent, the
# importer is rewritten, and the defect returns silently. The sentinel IS the state, so it
# is tracked.

# --- 2026-07-30 check-in sweep -------------------------------------------------
# Unity Technologies Particle Pack (191 MB / 886 files). Same policy as KayKit /
# polyperfect / Quaternius: git never holds the big source packs; it travels by
# zip / local copy. KEPT ON DISK as a build input -- NOT deleted.
# !! LOAD-BEARING AT RUNTIME: 54 owner-tagged keys in Assets/Editor/VfxManualPicks.json
# point into this tree, and Enemy.cs / PoiCalloutSystem.cs consume ParticlePack
# effects. A machine without the pack loses those VFX. Travel row added to
# tools/art/REQUIRED_PACKS.md; run tools/art/verify-runtime-art.ps1 on a fresh clone.
Assets/UnityTechnologies/
Assets/UnityTechnologies.meta

